# Chaos: wings with a part in front of the body (O583; client/BASE.md "0203"; src/client/chaoswinglayers.h (new, pure), outfit.cpp;
# after 0001-0202).
# Owner 2026-11-16: the code-drawn wings (O581) wrap the body: rings, orbits, feathers that cross the shoulder. The engine draws a
# look's wings once, before the body facing south or east and after it facing north or west, so a wing was either all behind or all
# in front. A wings look with two y patterns is now drawn twice in every direction: y 0 (the whole wing) before the body, y 1 (only
# the part in front) after it. A wings look with one y pattern is drawn as before. A client without this patch draws y 0 only, in
# the old order: the whole wing, behind the body facing south or east. The north / west placement moved into a lambda unchanged,
# because a layered wing needs it before the body too. The pair writes the patterns (client/tools/sprites/gen_drawn_wings.py apply).
diff -ruN a/src/client/chaoswinglayers.h b/src/client/chaoswinglayers.h
